    {
      "id": "47669803",
      "title": "Dijkstra Algorithm",
      "lectureOrder": 262,
      "videoOrder": 260,
      "sourceHash": "2357d6a6a963b73009c77b62b7f4baba5ebff41e99aa843de8035b1d52eb902b",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 5.21,
          "end": 5.75,
          "en": "All right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.75,
          "end": 9.02,
          "en": "In this lecture we are going to learn about Dijkstra's algorithm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.05,
          "end": 13.94,
          "en": "Dijkstra's algorithm is used to find the shortest path between the points on a graph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.97,
          "end": 17.48,
          "en": "So to understand how this is working let's look at the example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.48,
          "end": 19.46,
          "en": "So let's say we have a graph like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.46,
          "end": 22.7,
          "en": "So as you can see this is directed weighted graph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.7,
          "end": 27.17,
          "en": "So this means that in the H we have weight and we have the direction for h.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.17,
          "end": 31.76,
          "en": "So we can easily see that from a we can go to see b and d.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.76,
          "end": 34.61,
          "en": "And from B we can go to D and E.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.61,
          "end": 35.87,
          "en": "And it continues like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.87,
          "end": 39.14,
          "en": "Now every edge has weights that are assigned to them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.14,
          "end": 43.67,
          "en": "We are going to use the Dykstra's algorithm to find the shortest path between these edges.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.67,
          "end": 49.85,
          "en": "For example, if I take a as a source vertex and the destination vertex is e, so by using which route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.85,
          "end": 52.1,
          "en": "we can reach to the e in a shortest path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.1,
          "end": 55.37,
          "en": "So for this we are going to use the Dijkstra's algorithm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.37,
          "end": 60.56,
          "en": "Basically, Dijkstra's algorithm is an optimization problem where we want to minimize the sum of the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.56,
          "end": 60.86,
          "en": "edges.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.86,
          "end": 67.59,
          "en": "So initially if we take as a source vertex A, we don't know the distance from A to any other words",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 67.59,
          "end": 68.07,
          "en": "over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.07,
          "end": 73.83,
          "en": "So that's why initially A will be set to zero and other vertices will be set to infinity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.83,
          "end": 79.77,
          "en": "Because initially we know that every single vertex is infinitely far away from the starting point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 79.77,
          "end": 84.51,
          "en": "So basically this edge weights also shows the distance from the starting point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 84.51,
          "end": 89.61,
          "en": "So when we start our Dijkstra's algorithm, we are going to set the distance from the starting point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 89.64,
          "end": 91.62,
          "en": "to the given vertex to infinity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 91.62,
          "end": 96.33,
          "en": "Because when we start it, we don't know how far these vertices are located from a.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 96.36,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "Now at starting point, as I mentioned, it's going to be zero because we know that the distance between",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 104.46000000000001,
          "en": "the starting point to the starting point is going to be zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 104.46000000000001,
          "end": 107.88,
          "en": "So from A to A we can go to in zero units.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 113.61,
          "en": "Now after setting all distances from A to other vertices to infinity, first we are going to consider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 113.61,
          "end": 114.87,
          "en": "the neighbors of A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 114.9,
          "end": 119.91,
          "en": "Now we said that from A, we can go to B and c and D, so these are the neighbors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 119.91,
          "end": 125.31,
          "en": "Now here, after considering we are going to use the heap data structure, because in every iteration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 127.2,
          "en": "we are going to take the lowest value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 127.2,
          "end": 130.41,
          "en": "So minimum heap data structure is suitable for this problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 130.41,
          "end": 134.5,
          "en": "So we can get the minimum value in a constant running time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 134.5,
          "end": 138.01,
          "en": "So we are going to use the minimum heap that we created in previous sections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 138.01,
          "end": 140.23,
          "en": "So that's the data structure that we are going to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 140.23,
          "end": 143.32,
          "en": "But for now I just want to show the logic behind this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 143.32,
          "end": 145.75,
          "en": "Now the logic in Dijkstra's algorithm is like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 145.75,
          "end": 148.93,
          "en": "From A to B we are going in three units.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 148.93,
          "end": 153.49,
          "en": "So we are going to take zero plus three and we see that it is less than infinity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 153.49,
          "end": 159.31,
          "en": "So this means that we are going to go ahead and update the distance from A to B to three because it's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 159.31,
          "end": 160.48,
          "en": "less than the infinity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 160.48,
          "end": 163.27,
          "en": "Then we are going to do the same thing for the next neighbor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 163.27,
          "end": 164.89,
          "en": "So in the next neighbor we have C.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 164.89,
          "end": 167.47,
          "en": "So zero plus two is less than infinity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 167.47,
          "end": 170.71,
          "en": "So this means that the distance from A to C is going to be two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 170.74,
          "end": 173.56,
          "en": "Then we will consider the next neighbor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 173.56,
          "end": 177.64,
          "en": "So from A to D zero plus five is going to be the five units.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 177.64,
          "end": 179.77,
          "en": "So five is less than infinity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.8,
          "end": 181.63,
          "en": "We are going to update it to five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.63,
          "end": 185.35,
          "en": "So with this we have successfully considered the all neighbors of A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 185.38,
          "end": 188.56,
          "en": "So after this point to which vertex we will continue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 188.56,
          "end": 190.81,
          "en": "So we are going to continue to the minimum one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 190.81,
          "end": 196.78,
          "en": "So if we check the distances from A to B, we go to in three units from A to D, we go to in five units",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 196.78,
          "end": 199.27,
          "en": "and from A to C we go to in two units.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 199.27,
          "end": 201.91,
          "en": "So this means that we will continue to the C.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.91,
          "end": 205.06,
          "en": "So A will be considered and we will continue to do C.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.06,
          "end": 205.81,
          "en": "So in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 205.84,
          "end": 208.39,
          "en": "See also we are going to do the same logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.39,
          "end": 211.81,
          "en": "So two plus two is four which is less than five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.84,
          "end": 218.17000000000002,
          "en": "This means that from A to D the shortest path is going to be a c and D because four is less than five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.17000000000002,
          "end": 222.94,
          "en": "So we are going to update the distance from C to D to four.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 222.94,
          "end": 224.53,
          "en": "So it's going to be four.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.53,
          "end": 226.42000000000002,
          "en": "And we have only one neighbor of C.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 226.42000000000002,
          "end": 229.06,
          "en": "So that's why we have successfully considered this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 229.06,
          "end": 230.62,
          "en": "Then we will continue to the next node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 230.62,
          "end": 233.2,
          "en": "So as you can see we can continue to b and d.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 233.2,
          "end": 235.27,
          "en": "So B's value is three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.27,
          "end": 237.1,
          "en": "So this means that this is the minimum one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 237.1,
          "end": 238.9,
          "en": "We are going to continue to the b.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.9,
          "end": 243.55,
          "en": "So here from B we are going to consider the neighbors of B also.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 243.55,
          "end": 247.21,
          "en": "So from B we can go to D and we can go to E.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 247.33,
          "end": 250,
          "en": "So three plus one is going to be four.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 250,
          "end": 251.83,
          "en": "So four is equal to four.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.83,
          "end": 254.95,
          "en": "So we are not going to update the value of d over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.95,
          "end": 258.13,
          "en": "Then we will continue the distance of d over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258.13,
          "end": 259.9,
          "en": "Then we will continue to the next node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.93,
          "end": 261.46,
          "en": "Now in the next node we have e.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.55,
          "end": 265,
          "en": "So three plus five is eight which is less than infinity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 265,
          "end": 266.96,
          "en": "So we are going to update it to eight 8.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.99,
          "end": 271.64,
          "en": "Now, after doing so, you see that we have successfully reached the E, but we have another node over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 271.64,
          "end": 275.65999999999997,
          "en": "here which we have not visited yet, so we are going to continue to the minimum one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.65999999999997,
          "end": 277.85,
          "en": "So in this case we see that D is minimum.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 277.85,
          "end": 279.74,
          "en": "So we will continue to d.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.77,
          "end": 281.96,
          "en": "So from D we can go to E.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.99,
          "end": 283.90999999999997,
          "en": "So we are going to consider this edge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.90999999999997,
          "end": 287.78,
          "en": "So four plus three is going to be seven and seven is less than eight.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 287.78,
          "end": 291.56,
          "en": "So this means that we are going to update the distance of E to seven.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.56,
          "end": 297.2,
          "en": "So we have successfully visited all nodes and we have found the minimum distance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 297.23,
          "end": 303.62,
          "en": "Now minimum distance is going to be like this from A to E we need to go to C then we need to go to D.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 303.65,
          "end": 305.27,
          "en": "Then we need to go to E.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 305.3,
          "end": 310.28,
          "en": "So it's going to be a c d e because in this case the distance is going to be seven.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 310.28,
          "end": 311.54,
          "en": "And this is the minimum path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.57,
          "end": 315.35,
          "en": "Now for example if we want to go to B from A it's going to be this path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 315.35,
          "end": 320.78,
          "en": "If we want to go to from D we cannot go directly from A to D because this is going to cost five units.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 320.78,
          "end": 323.36,
          "en": "But if we go through C it's going to be four units.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 323.36,
          "end": 326.48,
          "en": "And if we go through B it's going to be the four units.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 326.48,
          "end": 330.17,
          "en": "So that's how the logic behind the Lycastus algorithm works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 330.2,
          "end": 333.89,
          "en": "Now we are going to take this logic and implement it in the code.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
